 Toniebox shows as offline in the tonies® app, you can usually fix this by reconnecting it to your known Wi-Fi network. Not sure how to do that? It's easy—simply follow the steps below. Reconnect to...\n\n### Playback Features: FAQ\n\nWe're delighted to be bringing you one of our most requested features. That's right, it is now possible to utilise the following features in app. 👀 Live Playback Status: See exactly which Tonie is on the box and view the chapter currently playing, right from your scree ⏸️ Pause and Play: Halt the a...\n\n### Can I manually turn off my Toniebox 2?\n\nYes, you can and here’s how: Lay the Toniebox face down on the speaker holes. Squeeze either ear for four seconds. The Toniebox 2 will then turn off. Alternatively: the Toniebox 2 automatically turns off after it’s been idle for five minutes. Please note: Manual switch off is not currently possible ...\n\n### Can I connect my Toniebox 2 to several different Wi-Fi networks?\n\nYour Toniebox 2 can store up to six different Wi-Fi networks. It will automatically connect to the network with the strongest available signal. Adding a New Network To connect your Toniebox 2 to another Wi-Fi network: Open the tonies® app. Tap Connect Toniebox, or go to Settings (top right corner). ...\n\n### How do I put my Toniebox 2 in Offline Mode?\n\nIf you would like to manually take your Toniebox 2 offline and stop it from searching for or connecting to available networks, you can do so by putting it into Offline Mode. This allows you to listen and play in with all previously downloaded content and disables Wi-Fi connection until you choose to...\n\n### How do I turn off the Toniebox 2?\n\nUnlike some gadgets with an “off” switch, the Toniebox 2 prefers to take matters into its own hands. If no stories, songs, or playtime magic are happening, it will gently nod off and turn itself off after about 5 minutes of quiet time. Simply remove any Tonie or Tonieplay game from the top of the To...\n\n### What features of the Toniebox 2 can I customise via the app?\n\nYou can personalise the Toniebox 2 listening experience with new and familiar features, all from the improved tonies® app. You can check the battery level, manage your Tonies collection and tweak settings right from your phone. And there's more to come – fresh features are being added all the time t...\n\n### Sleep Light with Timer & Sunrise Alarm guide\n\nThe Sleep Light with Timer helps little ones drift off with a soft, adjustable glow and a customisable timer. The Sunrise Alarm wakes them up with energising light and sound, staying gently lit until the alarm sounds. Please note: As the Sunrise Alarm requires connection to the charger it is only av...\n\n### What does the dynamic Light Ring do?\n\nThe new dynamic Light Ring does more than just look good... Our all new Light Ring lights up while your Tonie’s song or story plays, guides listeners through key moments such as connecting to Wi-Fi, adjusting volume with the Toniebox ears, powering down, and of course, exploring the all new world of...\n\n### Can I turn off the Light Ring?\n\nYes, you can adjust the brightness of the light ring continuously. If you set it to 0%, it is switched off. Please note: Tonieplay always needs the light ring to guide you through your Tonieplay experience.\n\n### How does the Toniebox 2 function differently in 1+ vs 3+ mode?\n\nFor safety reasons, some of the Toniebox 2’s features are limited in 1+ mode. 3+ Age Mode: 🎵 Can play while charging. 1+ Age Mode: ⚠️ Cannot play while charging and tilt to rewind or fast-forward is disabled.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSettings and Preferences – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-au/sections/29036413480082-Settings-and-Features)\nciteturn780search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Please note: Manual switch off is not currently possible ... ... Please note: Tonieplay always needs the light ring to guide you through your T